How to Run This Project

	1.	Initialize Terraform:
Run the following command to initialize the working directory and download the AWS provider:

terraform init

		2.	Validate Configuration:
Validate your configuration to ensure there are no syntax errors:

terraform validate

	3.	Plan the Deployment:
Generate and review the execution plan

	terraform plan

	
	4.	Apply the Configuration:
Deploy the resources to AWS:

  terraform apply 


	Type yes to confirm.

	5.	View Outputs:
After the deployment, view the outputs with:

	terraform outputs


1.	Push to GitHub:
	•	Create a .gitignore file and add the following to exclude sensitive files:

.terraform/
terraform.tfstate
terraform.tfstate.backup

•	Push your project to GitHub.

2.	Extend the Project:
	•	Add an Elastic IP for the instance.
	•	Attach a volume to the EC2 instance.
	•	Deploy a load balancer for multiple EC2 instances.
	
	
